  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "5401674",
      "title": "Adding Service Workers",
      "lectureOrder": 719,
      "videoOrder": 662,
      "sourceHash": "50e8d92c35f8b86f45820ac52e0198e79f7528df78cb57fbde62a7484ad93ca8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 3.75,
          "en": "-: Let's first of all understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.75,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "what a service worker actually is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 10.71,
          "en": "Now this is how our JavaScript code typically behaves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.71,
          "end": 12.42,
          "en": "It runs in a single thread.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.42,
          "end": 14.91,
          "en": "That means our web application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.91,
          "end": 17.52,
          "en": "which can consist of multiple pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.52,
          "end": 21.21,
          "en": "or, in the case of an Angular app, with one page only.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.21,
          "end": 24.81,
          "en": "This app often uses JavaScript and if you're using Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.81,
          "end": 26.28,
          "en": "you're, of course, using JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.28,
          "end": 28.8,
          "en": "because Angular uses JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.8,
          "end": 31.38,
          "en": "So this JavaScript code, the entire Angular app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 31.38,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "runs on one single thread and JavaScript has its features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 38.25,
          "en": "to still handle asynchronous code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.25,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "and not block the execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 42.12,
          "en": "But this is all normal JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.12,
          "end": 45.9,
          "en": "Now JavaScript and the browser also offers us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.9,
          "end": 48.42,
          "en": "to run an additional thread.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.42,
          "end": 51.42,
          "en": "We can run a so-called web worker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.42,
          "end": 54.24,
          "en": "and a special form of that is the service worker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 55.65,
          "en": "on another thread.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.65,
          "end": 58.44,
          "en": "So this still then uses one of the same thread",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.44,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "but it's a different thread than your main JavaScript code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 64.47,
          "en": "And the important part is that this thread",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 64.47,
          "end": 67.83,
          "en": "is kind of decoupled from your HTML pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 67.83,
          "end": 70.44,
          "en": "So this means that this can also continue running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 70.44,
          "end": 73.23,
          "en": "in the background, for example, on your mobile phone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 73.23,
          "end": 75.96000000000001,
          "en": "that is something mobile browsers typically offer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 75.96000000000001,
          "end": 77.88,
          "en": "This can continue running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 77.88,
          "end": 80.22,
          "en": "and could it could, therefore, also do advanced things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 80.22,
          "end": 82.8,
          "en": "like receive push notifications,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 82.8,
          "end": 84.96000000000001,
          "en": "take my full progressive web app course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 84.96000000000001,
          "end": 86.7,
          "en": "if you wanna learn more about this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 86.7,
          "end": 89.37,
          "en": "But one other crucial thing that a service worker can do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 92.58,
          "en": "is it can manage all your different pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.58,
          "end": 94.2,
          "en": "in case you got multiple pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.2,
          "end": 96.72,
          "en": "or your single page if you're building an Angular app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 96.72,
          "end": 100.92,
          "en": "And it can listen to outgoing networks request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.92,
          "end": 105.92,
          "en": "So it can listen to requests going out of your webpage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.93,
          "end": 108.24000000000001,
          "en": "For example, if you are fetching the assets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.24000000000001,
          "end": 112.2,
          "en": "of that webpage, the CSS code, the font, the JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 112.2,
          "end": 114.81,
          "en": "or also data from an API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.81,
          "end": 118.2,
          "en": "The service worker can catch these outgoing requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.2,
          "end": 119.55,
          "en": "and do something with them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 119.55,
          "end": 122.64,
          "en": "Like, for example, cache the responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 122.64,
          "end": 125.13,
          "en": "in a special cache storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 125.13,
          "end": 128.61,
          "en": "or then also return these cached responses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 128.61,
          "end": 131.22,
          "en": "back to your page so that it also works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 131.22,
          "end": 133.2,
          "en": "if you got no internet connection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 136.38,
          "en": "of course, only if there is a cached version available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 136.38,
          "end": 138.09,
          "en": "This is what the service worker does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 138.09,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "It can be seen as a proxy between your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 145.47,
          "en": "your front end app, and the HDP request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 145.47,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "you're sending to the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 149.85,
          "en": "It proxies that request, which means it caches it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 149.85,
          "end": 151.11,
          "en": "does something with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 151.11,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "and might then allow it to still go on and leave the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 156.54,
          "en": "but it could also block this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 156.54,
          "end": 159.75,
          "en": "Now configuring such a service worker and writing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 159.75,
          "end": 162.66,
          "en": "from scratch is something you can do and something you learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 162.66,
          "end": 164.97,
          "en": "in my full progressive web app course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 164.97,
          "end": 167.7,
          "en": "There you also learn about features like push notifications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 167.7,
          "end": 169.02,
          "en": "and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 169.02,
          "end": 171.78,
          "en": "For this video, we'll focus on how Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 171.78,
          "end": 176.1,
          "en": "can easily add such a service worker to our Angular app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 176.1,
          "end": 178.41,
          "en": "because it turns out that there is a special package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 178.41,
          "end": 179.67000000000002,
          "en": "we can install.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 179.67000000000002,
          "end": 181.41,
          "en": "For that, let's quit NG Serve.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 181.41,
          "end": 183.9,
          "en": "And now here it's important that you're using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 183.9,
          "end": 186.9,
          "en": "the latest CLI version for that project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 186.9,
          "end": 188.22,
          "en": "and this project does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 188.22,
          "end": 193.22,
          "en": "And then you can run NG add to add third party package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 194.19,
          "end": 196.5,
          "en": "but that's more than just a NPM library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 196.5,
          "end": 200.01,
          "en": "really some functionality to your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 200.01,
          "end": 204.03,
          "en": "and only some features can be edited because, essentially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 204.03,
          "end": 207,
          "en": "this will execute a command which has to be defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 207,
          "end": 209.73,
          "en": "by whichever package you are targeting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 209.73,
          "end": 211.82999999999998,
          "en": "So not every, not even close.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 211.82999999999998,
          "end": 215.16,
          "en": "not every third party library supports this feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 215.16,
          "end": 217.77,
          "en": "but there is a special library which does support it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 217.77,
          "end": 221.49,
          "en": "which you can target with add @angular/pwa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 221.49,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "And if you run this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 223.02,
          "end": 226.05,
          "en": "this will actually configure your existing project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 226.05,
          "end": 229.2,
          "en": "to use the Angular service worker package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 229.2,
          "end": 232.17000000000002,
          "en": "and start with a pre-configured service worker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 232.17000000000002,
          "end": 234.03,
          "en": "So it does a lot for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 234.03,
          "end": 235.98,
          "en": "You can already see it added some things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 235.98,
          "end": 239.01,
          "en": "to the index html file like the no script section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 239.01,
          "end": 241.05,
          "en": "to give a warning if JavaScript is turned off",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 241.05,
          "end": 244.2,
          "en": "because we need that, of course, we need that turned on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 244.2,
          "end": 247.65,
          "en": "It loads this manifest here, which it all generated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 247.65,
          "end": 251.22,
          "en": "Now that is important for actually having a launcher icon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 251.22,
          "end": 252.18,
          "en": "for your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 252.18,
          "end": 253.56,
          "en": "If you have it on a mobile phone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 253.56,
          "end": 255.06,
          "en": "you can even save it to the home screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 255.06,
          "end": 256.5,
          "en": "and then start it with that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 256.5,
          "end": 259.62,
          "en": "and you can define which icon that should use and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 259.62,
          "end": 261.63,
          "en": "So that is the manifest adjacent file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 261.63,
          "end": 264.21,
          "en": "Again, learn more in that course I mentioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 264.21,
          "end": 267.24,
          "en": "For us interesting is the app module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 267.24,
          "end": 268.62,
          "en": "because, in the app module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 268.62,
          "end": 270.84,
          "en": "we are using a service worker module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 270.84,
          "end": 273.78,
          "en": "which is imported from @angular service worker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 273.78,
          "end": 275.55,
          "en": "And this is really an official package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 275.55,
          "end": 278.52,
          "en": "of the Angular framework and it does what it sounds like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 278.52,
          "end": 281.01,
          "en": "It registers a service worker",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 281.01,
          "end": 284.76,
          "en": "which will be that proxy that catches outgoing requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 284.76,
          "end": 286.2,
          "en": "and does something with them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 286.2,
          "end": 288.51,
          "en": "and you will learn how to configure what it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 288.51,
          "end": 291.51,
          "en": "to them later in this video, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 291.51,
          "end": 293.85,
          "en": "We use it here by calling the register method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 293.85,
          "end": 298.44,
          "en": "And there we target the NGSW worker.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 298.44,
          "end": 301.05,
          "en": "and you won't find that file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 301.05,
          "end": 303.24,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 303.24,
          "end": 305.85,
          "en": "will actually be auto-generated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 305.85,
          "end": 308.58,
          "en": "it will be generated during the built process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 308.58,
          "end": 310.86,
          "en": "and it will be in the disc folder, therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 310.86,
          "end": 313.14,
          "en": "And it will hold your service worker,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 313.14,
          "end": 315.15,
          "en": "which will contain a lot of functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 315.15,
          "end": 317.61,
          "en": "which you don't have to, and typically don't want to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 317.61,
          "end": 319.23,
          "en": "write on your own.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 319.23,
          "end": 321.48,
          "en": "And here it's all the configured to only be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 321.48,
          "end": 323.343,
          "en": "if you're building for production.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 324.66,
          "end": 327.03,
          "en": "In the assets folder, we see some icons were added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 327.03,
          "end": 329.01,
          "en": "for that manifest adjacent file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 329.01,
          "end": 331.08,
          "en": "And in the root project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 331.08,
          "end": 333.63,
          "en": "we see that in the package adjacent file, something changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 333.63,
          "end": 336.42,
          "en": "For example, the Angular PWA package was added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 336.42,
          "end": 339.81,
          "en": "which includes that angular service worker package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 339.81,
          "end": 342.63,
          "en": "And we got this NGSW conflict file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 342.63,
          "end": 344.49,
          "en": "This is the file where you can configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 344.49,
          "end": 346.95,
          "en": "that service worker which will be generated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 346.95,
          "end": 349.44,
          "en": "but we'll take a closer look at this in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 349.44,
          "end": 352.95,
          "en": "The angular.json file, which manages to see live project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 352.95,
          "end": 355.14,
          "en": "also was adjusted a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 355.14,
